  "_doc": "UPDATE 05 section 6 VFX (T-095). Read by Effects (gravelight/autoload/effects.gd) and the helpers under gravelight/world/vfx/. quality: GLSettings vfx_quality low/medium/high scales particle counts, the pooled flash-light budget, casings per shot, the near snow and the dust motes. flash.classes: one muzzle flash look per weapon class (weapons.json 'class'); size scales the whole flash, length the petals along the barrel, petals the number of radial planes, core the front bloom, light/light_range the pooled OmniLight pulse, life seconds, smoke the wisp strength (0 = none), color the additive HDR tint; skip = no flash (the flamethrower has its own flame). upgraded_fringe tints a Crucible-taught weapon's petals; wonder weapons are violet Nachtglas. first_person: 'effects' = the world-space flash is drawn for the local player too and the viewmodel's own star is suppressed; 'holder' = leave the viewmodel flash to WeaponHolder. casings: the OGA cartridge set (models.json extras.cartridges.casing_for picks the node per weapon); kind_default maps the holder's casing kind (weapons.json feel.casing) to a node when the weapon is unknown. surfaces.name_hints: ordered [substring-of-collider-name, surface] pairs tried after the collider's 'surface' meta; the first match wins (gen_map00 merges the static meshes, so the colliders carry no material: names and metas are all there is). impacts: per surface the decal (an Effects.DECALS key, '' = the plain dark mark), the puff colours [start, end], the chunk mesh (size m, colour, emissive), how many chunks, sparks (bool) and whether the rise's dirt pool is used (snow/earth kind).",
